This builds a solid sandstone pyramid with a **51 × 51 base and 26 layers**, centered on the block containing the bot’s starting position. Run it inside an async function, as in your example.

```js
const position = world.getPosition(bot);
const centerX = Math.floor(position.x);
const centerZ = Math.floor(position.z);
const startY = Math.floor(position.y);

const baseSize = 51; // Keep odd for a single-block peak.
const halfBase = Math.floor(baseSize / 2);

for (let layer = 0; layer <= halfBase; layer++) {
    const radius = halfBase - layer;
    const y = startY + layer;

    for (let x = centerX - radius; x <= centerX + radius; x++) {
