sudo git -c user.name="Config Admin" \
  -c user.email="admin@example.com" \
  commit -m "Initial desktop configuration"
```

For Git-backed flakes, **new configuration files must be added to Git** before Nix will include them. Review files before publishing: hardware configuration may reveal disk identifiers, and configuration repositories must not contain secrets.

After editing:

```bash
sudo nixos-rebuild build --flake /etc/nixos#desktop
sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake /etc/nixos#desktop
```

To update within the selected release branches:

```bash
cd /etc/nixos
sudo nix flake update
sudo nixos-rebuild build --flake .#desktop
sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake .#desktop
```

Commit the resulting lock file after testing. When moving to another NixOS release, update both release branches together and read their release notes.

If the system becomes unusable, boot an older generation from the boot menu. From a working terminal, a system rollback is:

```bash
sudo nixos-rebuild switch --rollback
```

Rollback does not undo application data changes or every Home Manager side effect. Keep the configuration backup and avoid immediately deleting old generations.

