## My answer to the prompt

Let the final length be
\[
s=(n-1)\bmod k+1,
\]
and let \(q=(n-s)/k\) be the number of operations.

### Which elements can remain?

Use zero-based indices. If the surviving indices are
\[
p_0<p_1<\cdots<p_{s-1},
\]
then every gap before, between, and after survivors must contain a multiple of \(k\) deleted elements: an operation cannot cross an element that survives.

Consequently, the surviving indices have exactly the form
\[
p_i=i+k r_i,\qquad 0\le r_0\le r_1\le\cdots\le r_{s-1}\le q.
\]

Conversely, every such selection is achievable: each gap has length divisible by \(k\), so delete its elements in blocks of \(k\).

### Binary search and DP

For a candidate answer \(x\), mark an element as good if it is at least \(x\).

Because the problem uses the lower median, the final array must contain at least
\[
\left\lfloor s/2\right\rfloor+1
\]
good elements.

Process survivor positions \(i=0,\dots,s-1\). Let `dp[r]` be the maximum number of good elements selected so far when the latest chosen row is \(r\). The transition is
\[
\text{newDP}[r]=[a[i+kr]\ge x]+\max_{u\le r}\text{dp}[u].
\]

Prefix maxima compute one column in \(O(q+1)\). A feasibility check costs \(O(s(q+1))\), which is \(O(n)\), since \(s\le k\) and \(n=qk+s\).

### C++17 code

```cpp
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;

int main() {
    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);
    cin.tie(nullptr);

    int t;
    cin >> t;

    while (t--) {
        int n, k;
        cin >> n >> k;

        vector<int> a(n);
        int maximum = 0;
        for (int &v : a) {
            cin >> v;
            maximum = max(maximum, v);
        }

        int s = (n - 1) % k + 1;
        int q = (n - s) / k;
        int need = s / 2 + 1;

        vector<int> dp(q + 1);

        auto possible = [&](int x) {
            fill(dp.begin(), dp.end(), 0);

            for (int col = 0; col < s; ++col) {
                int best = 0;
                for (int row = 0; row <= q; ++row) {
                    // Read the previous column's value before replacing it.
                    best = max(best, dp[row]);
                    dp[row] = best + (a[col + row * k] >= x);
                }
            }

            return *max_element(dp.begin(), dp.end()) >= need;
        };

        int lo = 1, hi = maximum;
        while (lo < hi) {
            int mid = lo + (hi - lo + 1) / 2;
            if (possible(mid))
                lo = mid;
            else
                hi = mid - 1;
        }

        cout << lo << '\n';
    }
}
```

**Complexity:** \(O(n\log M)\) time per test case, where \(M=\max a_i\), and \(O(n)\) total memory including the input array.

